{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960197-2e-astral-ecstatic-wind","id":960197,"title":"[2E] Astral - Ecstatic Wind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-29T20:32:31-07:00","id":960197,"title":"[2E] Astral - Ecstatic Wind","content":"I'm preparing to run game in deep Astral ( Sidereal Wastes, to be precises ) but still could not get how rules for Ecstatic Wind work in 2E ( page 250 of new corebook should answer it ). We have table with sections like 'Typical Wind Strength' and 'Damage', but rules do not say anything more than this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw, page 250</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a mage is killed by Ecstatic Wind, she returns with the Soul Shocked Condition and loses a Willpower dot due to depersonalization. Finally, since her soul momentarily escapes its usual confines of self to be smeared across raw celestial Being, it often brings back some sign of its deformity: a Paradox Condition (see p.116). This crosses metaphysical lines and can even affect the mage\u2019s physical body and surroundings. The Condition resolves itself as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we do not have detailing if rolled by Gnosis + 1/2/3 Damage is Bashing, Lethal or Aggravated to character. Also how many times Amnion can be summoned. Or does this 'armor' is destroyed with enough Damage from Ecstatic Wind.<br /> <br /> <b>Bonus question:</b> <b>In what intervals I should roll on the Ecstatic Wind on the planet's surface in the Sidereal Wastes?</b> PCs will explore grounds of cursed long star, but they will not travel by thought, like Astral is described normally her - rather, they will use normal game world means of travel - walking, jumping, maybe driving some vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-29-2016, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T22:27:06-07:00","id":960243,"title":"","content":"Not sure about what kind of damage it should be,<br /> but the chart says you should be rolling damage every Action in the Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Time is strange there.<br /> A conversation could kill the party with everyone's reply being an action, one person speaks - Winds, someone replies - Winds, Someone makes a pun in response - Winds.<br /> Traveling for a year with one simple action could be less damaging to them, if they arent required rolls to get over rough terrain along the way.<br /> <br /> That's how I understand it at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T02:22:31-07:00","id":960312,"title":"","content":"The damage is to dream health. I believe you just lose dream health and there is no distinction of B/L/A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:44:13-07:00","id":961018,"title":"","content":"Mrmdubois has it right; it's dream health. The Amnion, meanwhile, can be summoned and retracted as often as desired. It's not really armour, per se; it's just the universe saying &quot;You're a part of me!&quot;, and the Mage's massive, raging ego sticking out its tongue to say &quot;No I'm not!&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Ecstatic Wind's roll intervals, I think that's largely up to you, as it depends on the narrative structure of your game. The default in the Sidereal Wastes is that it's once per actions <i>but</i> in the Wastes, actions are defined as any narratively-linked series of events, regardless of time involved. For example, building a castle by oneself - an act which takes subjective centuries - is one action, but so is a conversation that takes minutes (or even each social roll in the conversation). Indeed, from the perspectives of the respective parties, the castle builder might spend years building a castle, only to find his friends are still only just beginning to discuss what to do with their discoveries.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't work for you - it can make for very short Astral sojourns, especially for low Gnosis player characters - then just adjust as needed. Perhaps the planet provides a buffer of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}